# struct cfl_variant Definition

The structure contains a type field, a size field, a `referenced` flag, and a union holding the actual data. Here it is:

```c
struct cfl_variant {
    int type;
    size_t size;
    uint8_t referenced;

    /* the data */
    union {
        cfl_sds_t as_string;
        cfl_sds_t as_bytes;
        unsigned int as_bool;
        int64_t as_int64;
        uint64_t as_uint64;
        double as_double;
        void *as_reference;
        struct cfl_array *as_array;
        struct cfl_kvlist *as_kvlist;
    } data;
};
```

The `referenced` field indicates whether data is being referenced ("CFL_TRUE") or owned by the variant ("CFL_FALSE"). Per the header comment, referenced data "uses less memory, when the variant is not referenced we use a copy of the original data."

